{:edb/db-before-t 1467 :edb/db-after-t 1468 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534780 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:41:51.493Z" 13194139534780 true] [17592186078455 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309788 13194139534780 true] [17592186078455 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309795 13194139534780 true] [17592186078476 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309799 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309789 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1089 "q-107060" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4}=$" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1113 #uuid "e9530e94-2077-5cc5-bfa5-d3da05501ed7" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309788 1145 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}-1}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2x-7}-1)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{2x-7})}^{2}-{1}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-7-1}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-8}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2(x-4)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309790 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309791 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309792 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309793 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309794 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1041 "selection" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309792 13194139534780 true] [17592186309789 1110 #uuid "34a2c02c-86e3-5c46-9a01-8a0355ee52d9" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309790 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309790 1111 #uuid "f0f1c010-5011-5481-80a3-0cb47f139182" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309791 1034 "2" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309791 1111 #uuid "b9a5187b-9604-5273-b91a-7be182b0cb4a" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309792 1034 "1" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309792 1111 #uuid "ce55d0f9-0f9c-5ff3-bcb6-f447db927598" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309793 1034 "-4" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309793 1111 #uuid "da8005e6-e2e8-5d45-ba27-fd29abaeb9ae" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309794 1034 "4" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309794 1111 #uuid "680995e6-a209-5e11-a827-cf8d8c1e6261" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309796 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1089 "q-338477" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1113 #uuid "060847a0-f068-589c-94fd-9b85a0de164c" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309795 1145 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & =\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5(5)}}{5-5}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{(5-\\sqrt{5x})(5+\\sqrt{5x})}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{{5}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5x})}^{2}}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{25-5x}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5(5-x)}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5\\cancel{(5-x)}}{\\cancel{(5-x)}(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5(5)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309797 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309798 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1041 "field-1" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309797 13194139534780 true] [17592186309796 1110 #uuid "2466bdcc-8923-54b6-89fe-6cd1638dce50" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309797 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309797 1111 #uuid "f91dc651-1dcb-55c0-ad58-2fb6f060c3e7" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309798 1034 "1" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309798 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309798 1111 #uuid "1b842499-2b2e-53b1-82ab-9f617a433e0e" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309800 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1089 "q-338504" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1113 #uuid "25bce61b-a5f1-5031-96bf-625853eef9f9" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309799 1145 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=3$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & =\\frac{3-3}{3(3)-\\sqrt{27(3)}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x-\\sqrt{27x})(3x+\\sqrt{27x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{27x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9{x}^{2}-27x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x(x-3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{27x}}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3)+\\sqrt{27(3)}}{9(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+9}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309800 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309801 13194139534780 true] [17592186309800 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534780 true] [17592186309800 1041 "field-1" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309800 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309801 13194139534780 true] [17592186309800 1110 #uuid "99721541-de5a-5611-85b3-e921e432021d" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309801 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534780 true] [17592186309801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534780 true] [17592186309801 1111 #uuid "573c49ce-e5d8-54dd-897a-3b5674cac952" 13194139534780 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-107060" 17592186309788 "q-107060/selection" 17592186309789 "q-107060/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" 17592186309790 "q-107060/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" 17592186309791 "q-107060/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186309792 "q-107060/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc